        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Use the binomial expansion formula: <math>$(a + b)^n = \\sum_{k=0}^n \binom{n}{k} a^{n-k} b^k$</math>.<br>Here, <math>$a = 2x$</math>, <math>$b = -3$</math>, and <math>$n = 5$</math>.<br>The term containing <math>$x^3$</math> is <math>$\binom{5}{2} (2x)^3 (-3)^2$</math>.<br>Calculate: <math>$\binom{5}{2} = 10$</math>, <math>$(2x)^3 = 8x^3$</math>, and <math>$(-3)^2 = 9$</math>.<br>Thus, the coefficient is <math>$10 \times 8 \times 9 = 720$</math>.</p>",
